  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="2.091969" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-ngc4214&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:33:57+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="CVN" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="36.278393487892025" Magnitude="0" Name="Dwarf Galay NGC 4214" Opacity="100" RA="12.258223317713913" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-ngc4214/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="2.091969">
    <Description>This image was obtained with the wide-field view of the Mosaic camera on the Mayall 4-meter telescope at Kitt Peak National Observatory. NGC 4214 is a dwarf galaxy that is much smaller than our own galaxy, the Milky Way. Despite its small size, NGC 4214 is undergoing vigorous star formation, made visible by the many red clouds of hydrogen gas. NGC 4214 has a companion, the very small galaxy UGCA 276, which is faintly visible in the upper-right corner of the picture. The image was generated with observations in B (blue), V (cyan), I (orange) and H-alpha (red) filters. This image is rotated counterclockwise 55 degrees from North is up, East is left.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet BandPass="Visible" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.5947392" BaseTileLevel="0" BottomsUp="False" CenterX="183.79295242475254" CenterY="36.217979383717896" DataSetType="Sky" ElevationModel="False" FileType=".png" Generic="False" Name="Dwarf Galay NGC 4214" OffsetX="-0.082320886975" OffsetY="-0.033457115043" Projection="Tan" QuadTreeMap="" Rotation="-65.05201135244815" Sparse="True" StockSet="False" TileLevels="5" Url="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-ngc4214/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" WidthFactor="2" Xastropix_ids="noirlab|noao-ngc4214" Xcxstatus="in:642762d1975014bc743f1724">
        <Credits>T.A. Rector (University of Alaska Anchorage) and H. Schweiker (WIYN and NOIRLab/NSF/AURA)</Credits>
        <CreditsUrl>https://noirlab.edu/public/images/noao-ngc4214/</CreditsUrl>
        <ThumbnailUrl>http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-ngc4214/thumb.jpg</ThumbnailUrl>
      </ImageSet>
    </ForegroundImageSet>
  </Place>
  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;iotw2048a&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-11-25T16:00:00+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="MON" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="-6.3822641243103915" Magnitude="0" Name="Colorful Cosmic Reflections" Opacity="100" RA="6.130330133033842" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/iotw2048a/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="2.0937403776098">
    <Description>This striking image, streaked with bright swathes of color, captures the beautiful reflection nebula NGC 2170. The diffuse clouds of interstellar dust in the nebula scatter and reflect light from nearby stars, creating this vividly colorful scene. Dust grains reflect blue light from hot stars embedded in the nebula. And warm hydrogen gas glows a deep red. Seen as dark tendrils, dust also absorbs the light from stars and gas behind it. This particular nebula lies in the constellation Monoceros (The Unicorn) — a faint constellation on the celestial equator. It was observed using the SMARTS 0.9-meter Telescope at Cerro Tololo Inter-American Observatory in Chile, a Program of NSF’s NOIRLab.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet BandPass="Visible" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.228348845647872" BaseTileLevel="0" BottomsUp="False" CenterX="91.9548394498" CenterY="-6.38237527195" DataSetType="Sky" ElevationModel="False" FileType=".png" Generic="False" Name="Colorful Cosmic Reflections" OffsetX="0.000111498459789" OffsetY="0.000111498459789" Projection="Tan" QuadTreeMap="" Rotation="90.17999999999996" Sparse="True" StockSet="False" TileLevels="3" Url="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/iotw2048a/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" WidthFactor="2" Xastropix_ids="noirlab|iotw2048a" Xcxstatus="in:6427625f975014bc743f1632">
        <Credits>CTIO/NOIRLab/NSF/AURA Acknowledgments: Travis Rector (University of Alaska Anchorage), Mahdi Zamani &amp;amp; Davide de Martin</Credits>
        <CreditsUrl>https://noirlab.edu/public/images/iotw2048a/</CreditsUrl>
        <ThumbnailUrl>http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/iotw2048a/thumb.jpg</ThumbnailUrl>
      </ImageSet>
    </ForegroundImageSet>
  </Place>
