  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-m95_2&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:53:17.340523+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="LEO" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="11.709153575822349" Magnitude="0" Name="M95, NGC 3351" Opacity="100" RA="10.732481372338807" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-m95_2/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="2.1250679999999997">
    <Description>The SBb barred spiral galaxy M95, possibly ringed, is a member of the Leo I galaxy grouping, which includes M96, and M105, as well as various NGC and other galaxies, all at a distance of about 38 million light-years. This picture was taken in December 1994 at the KPNO 0.9-meter telescope and shows the fainter outer regions of the galaxy, as well as various small faint background galaxies. A different view at higher resolution also shows the complex inner structure. Image size 7.9x12.5 arc minutes.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet BandPass="Visible" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.3878912" BaseTileLevel="0" BottomsUp="False" CenterX="161.0028226" CenterY="11.76803532" DataSetType="Sky" ElevationModel="False" FileType=".png" Generic="False" Name="M95, NGC 3351" OffsetX="0.015482756990579993" OffsetY="-0.058827665569" Projection="Tan" QuadTreeMap="" Rotation="-0.20017647147236012" Sparse="True" StockSet="False" TileLevels="4" Url="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-m95_2/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" WidthFactor="2" Xastropix_ids="noirlab|noao-m95_2" Xcxstatus="in:642762c3975014bc743f1706">
