  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-02338&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:33:57+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="UMA" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="53.06845644574611" Magnitude="0" Name="NGC 3718 in Ursa Major" Opacity="100" RA="11.542980476215327" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-02338/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="2.1776999999999997">
    <Description>NGC3718 is an unusual lenticular galaxy of type S0(pec), in the constellation Ursa Major. It has a number of unusual absorption features. KPNO 4-meter Mayall telescope, 1975.</Description>
