  </Place>
  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-02345&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:33:46.935532+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="COM" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="27.98298369609153" Magnitude="0" Name="Cluster of galaxies in Coma Berenices" Opacity="100" RA="12.994669950145262" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-02345/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="2.55">
    <Description>The Coma Berenices cluster of galaxies contains more than 1000 galaxies, with a large number of E (elliptical) and S0 (lenticular) types. KPNO 4-meter Mayall telescope, 1974.</Description>
