  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-02272&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:33:50+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="CVN" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="47.19614899495245" Magnitude="0" Name="M51, the Whirlpool Nebula, NGC 5194/5195" Opacity="100" RA="13.497995944774344" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-02272/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="3.493499999999999">
    <Description>The Whirlpool Nebula in the constellation Canes Venatici was the first in which spiral structure was clearly seen. It is actually a pair of interacting galaxies. Kitt Peak 4-meter Mayall telescope, 1975.</Description>
