  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="3.9429119999999998" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-comacol&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:33:46.854721+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="COM" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="27.98116879292872" Magnitude="0" Name="Cluster of galaxies in Coma Berenices" Opacity="100" RA="13.00293168643313" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-comacol/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="3.9429119999999998">
    <Description>The Coma Berenices cluster of galaxies contains more than 1000 galaxies, with a large number of E (elliptical) and S0 (lenticular) types. The color image was created from three separate exposures taken in blue, red and almost-infrared light, using the Kitt Peak National Observatory&amp;#x27;s 0.9-meter telescope.</Description>
