  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="-6.211799999999999" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-m78&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2006-08-09T12:13:35+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="ORI" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="0.0929014996881184" Magnitude="0" Name="M78, NGC 2068" Opacity="100" RA="5.77333319644486" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-m78/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="4.28608643911722">
    <Description>This image of M78, the brightest diffuse reflection nebula in the sky, was taken in 2006 with the Mosaic imager on the Mayall 4-meter telescope on Kitt Peak. Located some 1600 light-years away and around 4 light-years across, M78 is part of the Orion complex, a large region of star-forming gas and dust.</Description>
