  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-ngc3582&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:34:09+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="CAR" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="-61.22152839667299" Magnitude="0" Name="NGC 3582 in Sagittarius" Opacity="100" RA="11.205855063363368" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-ngc3582/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="4.572146161331999">
    <Description>NGC3582 is a minor nebula in the Sagittarius arm of the Milky Way galaxy. It is part of star-forming region RCW 57 in Carina. This image was taken in 2007 using the Mosaic-2 imager on the Blanco 4-meter telescope at Cerro Tololo Inter-American Observatory.</Description>
