  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="8.822999999999999" Annotation="{&quot;channel&quot;: &quot;noirlab&quot;, &quot;itemid&quot;: &quot;noao-02346&quot;, &quot;publishedUTCISO8601&quot;: &quot;2020-06-30T21:34:01+00:00&quot;}" Constellation="VIR" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="12.8509992785441" Magnitude="0" Name="Cluster of galaxies in Virgo" Opacity="100" RA="12.4418708398052" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="http://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/noirlab/noao-02346/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="5.64672">
    <Description>The Virgo cluster of galaxies includes M84 and M86. Thousands of galaxies form a rich, loose, irregular cluster which is not strongly concentrated towards the center. KPNO 4-meter Mayall telescope, 1974. See also this Schmidt image.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
